# Scoped deliberately to ONE path. The repo otherwise relies on git's default line-ending
# handling (core.autocrlf), and a broader rule here would rewrite endings across the tree.

# Firebase's sign-in helper, vendored verbatim so the installed iOS app can complete a Google
# handshake first-party (docs/runbooks/firebase-auth-helper-selfhost.md). `-text` disables all
# line-ending conversion: these files must stay byte-identical to what Firebase serves, because
# re-syncing them is a plain re-download and the staleness check compares them against upstream.
# Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF and every future comparison reports a
# difference that is not one — which would make a genuinely stale helper indistinguishable from
# a freshly synced one.
public/__/** -text

# Agent tooling scripts must check out with LF on every platform. The Workflow runner refuses a
# script containing control characters, and on a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) a plain
# `text` file arrives with CRLF — which made `/full-debug-sweep` unable to launch its own
# reasoning workflow by name until the file was hand-normalised (full-sweep-2026-09-05).
.claude/workflows/*.js text eol=lf
.claude/commands/*.md text eol=lf
